    "title": "bip85: Say when applications must use BIP85-DRNG",
    "user": {
      "login": "BenWestgate",
      "id": 73506583,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjczNTA2NTgz",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73506583?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/BenWestgate",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/BenWestgate/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "There has been confusion during bip85 app proposals which entropy source to use, lets make their choice explicit in the standard.\n\n**What:** An application that could need more than the 64 bytes of HMAC-SHA512 output for any of its derivation paths MUST use BIP85-DRNG for all of its derivation paths. All other applications MUST use the HMAC-SHA512 output directly.\n\n**How:** Two sentences after the paragraph that introduces the HMAC output, a one-line rationale footnote, the version bump and a changelog entry.\n\n**Why:** This is the per-application rule akarve proposed on https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/2295 (Sep 19 and Oct 12, 2026). Every existing application already follows it: RSA and DICE use BIP85-DRNG, and BIP39, HD-Seed WIF, XPRV, HEX, PWD BASE64, PWD BASE85 and Nostr never read more than the 64 bytes. No output changes. A new MUST is a backward-compatible change to the specification, so this is a MINOR bump to 2.2.0 per BIP 3.",
