      "updated_at": "2026-10-20T17:03:20Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Concept ACK. An independent implementation, btclib-wallet's `bip85.py`, already follows the rule: only DICE and RSA read BIP85-DRNG, and every other application uses the HMAC output directly, so no output changes. Its 65 BIP85 tests, which include every vector the BIP publishes, pass. The RSA section still says the key generator \"should\" use BIP85-DRNG; a \"MUST\" there would match the new rule.\n",
